    "observation": "A zero-plan-miss attempt gives about 40% faster AVX32 formatting but changes the Clang14 iterator lowering and thousands of linked positions. Nine predeclared native/mixed observations lose more than 1%; the candidate is held.",
    "hypothesis": "Use the existing two 32-bit C4/C5 plan cells and existing vector call. Redirect only that call to a same-signature tail selector, preserving the ordinary iterator and every other original runtime object. Original option/callback checks remain their sole owner. Non-vector and no-plan instructions pay no new attempt.",
    "scope": "Clang-only prototype on the newly published alias baseline; GCC keeps both plan cells zero and its original call target.",
